 New Zealand peritoneal dialysis patient populations</article-title><source>J Am Soc Nephrol</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>278</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306167</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tonelli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hemmelgarn</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Manns</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Use and outcomes of peritoneal dialysis among Aboriginal people in Canada</article-title><source>J Am Soc Nephrol</source><year>2005</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>482</fpage><lpage>488</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15590757</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obesity is associated with worse peritoneal dialysis outcomes in the Australia and New Zealand patient populations</article-title><source>J Am Soc Nephrol</source><year>2003</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>2894</fpage><lpage>2901</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14569099</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huisman</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieuwenhuizen</surname><given-names>MGM</given-names></name><name><surname>Th de Charro</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient-related and centre-related factors influencing technique survival of peritoneal dialysis in The Netherlands</article-title><source>Nephrol Dial Transplant</source><year>2